  "notes": "WORD FORMATION: From {飯|まま} (cooked rice, meal) with vowel change for baby talk.\n\nUSAGE: One of the earliest words Japanese babies learn to say, along with ママ (mama) and パパ (papa).\n\nNOTE: Not to be confused with the adverb まんま (as is, unchanged), which has different origins.\n\nRELATED BABY TALK WORDS:\n- おてて (hands)\n- おめめ (eyes)\n- あんよ (feet/walking)\n- ねんね (sleep)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ごはん (rice, meal - neutral)\n- {食事|しょくじ} (meal - formal)",
